Paragraph 2
Section/subsection name: Paragraph 2
Content:

Based on this definition, when κ=1, the task reduces to identifying the exact i-th ranked element. As shown in Appendix L, finding p(i)in high-dimensional spaces is challenging, as its complexity is tied to that of the half-space range counting problem [2,26]. For 1<κ≪n, this formulation naturally leads to a relaxed variant of the problem: instead of returning a single point, the output is a small set that is guaranteed to contain p(i). Inspired by the notion of conformal prediction in machine learning [8,85], we refer to this set as the conformal set for ranki.6

